This package contains a bounded WebAssembly Windows installer inspector built
on the following permissively licensed Rust crates (exact versions pinned in
Cargo.lock):

  cfb 0.14.0                 MIT               https://github.com/mdsteele/rust-cfb
  msi 0.10.0                 MIT               https://github.com/mdsteele/rust-msi
  cab 0.6.0                  MIT               https://github.com/mdsteele/rust-cab
  lzxd 0.2.7                 MIT OR Apache-2.0 https://github.com/mdsteele/rust-lzxd
  flate2 1.1.x               MIT OR Apache-2.0 (pure-Rust miniz_oxide backend)
  miniz_oxide                MIT
  data-encoding 2.11.1       MIT
  serde / serde_json         MIT OR Apache-2.0
  sha2 0.10.9                MIT OR Apache-2.0
  wasm-bindgen 0.2.108       MIT OR Apache-2.0
  encoding_rs 0.8.41         (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause
  uuid / byteorder / time    MIT OR Apache-2.0

No GPL, LGPL, copyleft, or proprietary code is linked into the distributed
module. Cabinet Quantum decompression is intentionally unsupported
(unsupported_compression); MSZIP and stored members decode through flate2/
miniz_oxide and LZX members through the pure-Rust lzxd crate.

Turen added the bounded WebAssembly wrapper (msi_inspect / msi_stream_read /
cab_list / cab_extract). The wrapper code is Apache-2.0 OR MIT, copyright
2026 Turen Labs.
